        "stop_reason": {
          "kind": "finished",
          "message": "Implemented a real INI parser + printer in MoonBit for the dialect in `specs/ini.md`, completing the declarations in `ini_spec.mbt` (which is untouched).\n\n## What was built\n\n| File | Responsibility |\n| --- | --- |\n| `ini.mbt` | `pub fn parse`: logical-line classification (blank / comment / section / entry), document assembly (global map + section map, last-wins duplicates, re-opened sections) |\n| `scanner.mbt` | whitespace/char classes, LF+CRLF line splitting, first-separator scan, trailing-backslash run counting, char-array view helper |\n| `value.mbt` | value carriers: quoted values (same-line close, escapes), unquoted values (inline-comment stripping, backslash continuations), per-carrier escape tables |\n| `section.mbt` | section headers: bracket scan, name trim, wrapping-quote strip, exactness checks |\n| `printer.mbt` | `pub fn print`: always-double-quoted values with escapes, section names quoted only when needed, stable sorted output |\n| `errors.mbt` | `syntax_error` raising `Failure(\"INI parse error on line N: …\")` |\n| `ini_extra_test.mbt` | 70 added black-box tests, one per dialect rule (run table, escape tables, comments, quotes, sections, CRLF, real-world samples, invalid inputs) |\n| `README.md` | overview, architecture, pipeline, algorithms, usage, testing, design decisions |\n\nKey semantic points: continuation is decided on the **raw** line by the parity of the trailing backslash run (odd = marker, even = escaped literals); only the first physical line of a continued value is read as syntax (continuation lines contribute text); trimming happens before escape decoding so a decoded `\\n` survives; each carrier decodes only its own escapes (`\\\\ \\n \\r \\t`, plus `\\\"` in `\"…\"`, only `\\\\`/`\\'` in `'…'`) and keeps everything else verbatim.\n\nOne non-obvious bug found and fixed: `StringView` mixes index spaces (`length()`, `get_char`, slicing are UTF-16 code units; `iter2` yields character indices), which broke values/keys containing a surrogate pair (e.g. an emoji made a quoted value look unterminated). Scanning now works on `Array[Char]` runs with `view_of` rebuilding views.\n\n## Verification (commands actually run)\n\n- `moon test` — **82/82 pass**, repeated 5× (the QuickCheck round-trip property is randomized) plus once on `--target js`.\n- `moon check` — 0 errors, **0 warnings**; `pkg.generated.mbti` is current (`moon info` is not on this sandbox's allowlist; `moon check` regenerates the same file, whose public API is exactly `parse`, `print`, `Doc`).\n- `moon fmt --check` — clean.\n- Independent explore-agent audit of the implementation against `specs/ini.md`: no panics found in any malformed input it tried, and the run-length table, escape tables, comment rules, key/section validation and round-trip were confirmed conformant. Its remaining findings were spec ambiguities plus two printer limits (a section name holding `[`/`]`, or both quote characters while needing a carrier, cannot be represented) — documented in the README; neither is reachable from `parse` output or the QuickCheck generators. Its CRLF observation (a line containing only a stray CR should be blank) was fixed by widening the dialect whitespace set to ASCII whitespace.\n\nCaveats: behaviour in genuinely ambiguous corners follows the spec's explicit wording (e.g. a continuation marker is counted on the raw line even if it sits inside an inline comment), and the withheld private suite cannot be run here."
