          "message": "## Done — INI parser implemented, all gates green\n\n### Deliverable\n\n| File | Role |\n| --- | --- |\n| `scanner.mbt` (113 L) | line splitting (LF/CRLF, no phantom final line), whitespace trimming, inline-comment cut, trailing-backslash runs |\n| `section.mbt` (80 L) | `[header]` scanning: name to the first `]`, trailing text must be whitespace/comment, no nested `[`, blank rejected, whole-name quote pair stripped without re-trimming |\n| `value.mbt` (190 L) | `Carrier` enum (`Bare`/`Double`/`Single`), same-line quote scanning, per-carrier escape decoding, continuation joining (odd/even backslash runs on raw text) |\n| `ini.mbt` (101 L) | driver: line classification, first `=`/`:` separator, key validation (non-empty, no control chars), `Doc` assembly with last-wins and section re-open |\n| `printer.mbt` (114 L) | deterministic sorted output; values always double-quoted with `\\ \" LF CR TAB` escaped; section names quoted when parsing would otherwise alter them |\n| `ini_local_test.mbt` | 54 black-box conformance tests (`local/`-prefixed names and helpers so they cannot collide with the withheld suite) |\n| `README.md`, `README.mbt.md` | architecture, approach, usage, testing, design decisions, known limits |\n\n`ini_spec.mbt`, `ini_qc.mbt`, `ini_pub_test.mbt`, `specs/` and `moon.mod` are untouched (verified line-for-line). `pkg.generated.mbti` is in sync.\n\n### Validation actually run (in `tasks/ini_run_3`)\n\n- `moon test` → **66 tests, 66 passed, 0 failed** (all 12 public cases incl. both property tests, plus 54 local ones).\n- `moon check --deny-warn` → exit 0, **zero warnings**.\n- `moon fmt` then `moon fmt --check` → exit 0, nothing pending.\n- `moon info` is blocked by this sandbox's spawn allowlist; `moon check` performs the same interface refresh, and `pkg.generated.mbti` matches the API.\n- `moon fmt` could not reformat the provided files (already formatted); behaviour was covered by tests derived from `specs/ini.md` (escape table per carrier, continuation run lengths N=1–4, CRLF, unicode, git-config/systemd/php.ini shapes, all required rejections), a 150-document fuzz round trip (values include `= : ; # \" ' \\`, LF, CR, NUL, DEL, emoji; names sometimes quote-wrapped or space-padded), a 500-input syntax-garbage fuzz proving no input panics, a 50-line continuation chain, and a 1000-case `parse(print(doc)) == doc` property run.\n\n### Independent audits\n\nTwo review subagents audited the work. No blockers; the findings were fixed or documented: the printer now re-quotes section names whose surrounding quotes/whitespace the parser would otherwise consume (so `[\"\"x\"\"]` → `\"x\"` and ` padded ` round-trip), headers end at their **first** `]` (so `[a] ; see [b]` is the section `a`), a `[` inside a name has its own error message, and the README/known-limits prose matches the code.\n\n### Notes / caveats\n\n- Two dialect choices are conscious readings of `specs/ini.md`: a continuation marker at end of input is an error whether or not the file ends with a newline; and `[\" a \"]` names ` a ` (only the quote pair is removed, no second trim).\n- Keys whose first character is `;`, `#` or `[`, keys containing `=`/`:`, and section names containing `[`/`]` have no INI spelling at all — `parse` never produces them and the contract excludes them; this is documented.\n- `edits.json` (contents `[]`) is a leftover temporary batch file in the task directory; the `remove` tool refused it (\"not recorded as created by the agent this session, no approval channel\"), so it was left neutered rather than deleted."
